>> title: Harvest Bowl
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: chicken, sweet potato, wild rice, bowl, sheet pan, autumn
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: harvest bowl, wild rice bowl, autumn bowl, fall harvest bowl, roast chicken and sweet potato bowl, grain bowl, buddha bowl, power bowl
>> pairs-with: basic-vinaigrette
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr 15 min
>> slack: forgiving — the rice, the sweet potato and the chicken all hold an hour in a low oven; only the greens wilt, and they go in last
>> step.1: The wild rice goes in hot enough to soften the kale under it and take the edge off the goat cheese.
>> step.2: simmer 45 min, until the grains split
>> step.3: roast 425°F (220°C) 30 min, cut side down
>> step.4: roast 425°F (220°C) 25 min
>> step.5: shred it hot, dress it hot
>> step.6: build it warm

A warm bowl, not a salad. The wild rice goes in hot enough to soften the kale under it and to take the edge off the goat cheese, which is the whole difference between this and the same six things cold.

Simmer @wild rice{1%cup}(190 g; rinsed) in @salted chicken broth{3%cups}(710 mL) in a #saucepan{} ~simmer{45%min}, until the grains split open and curl, then drain off whatever is left.

Roast @sweet potatoes{1 1/2%lb}(680 g; in 3/4-inch cubes) tossed with @olive oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) and @kosher salt{3/4%tsp} on a #sheet pan{} at 425°F (220°C) ~roast{30%min}, in one layer and not stirred for the first twenty, so the faces against the pan go dark.

Roast @chicken thighs{1 1/2%lb}(680 g; boneless, skin on) rubbed with @olive oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL) and @kosher salt{1%tsp} at 425°F (220°C) ~roast{25%min}, until the skin is crisp and the juices run clear.

Pull @&(~1)chicken{} into rough shreds with two forks and toss it, still hot, with @cider vinegar{1%Tbs}(15 mL) and @whole grain mustard{2%tsp} — hot meat drinks a dressing, cold meat only sits in it.

Spoon @&(~4)wild rice{} into four bowls, pile @&(~3)roasted sweet potato{} and @&(~1)dressed chicken{} on top, and finish with @baby kale{4%cups}(packed), @apple{1}(cored and sliced thin), @goat cheese{3%oz}(90 g; crumbled) and @balsamic vinaigrette{1/3%cup}(80 mL).
